body:
Consider adding validation for the `handler` field type. The current implementation accepts both `RouteHandler` (function) and `string` (handler name), but when a string is provided, the `resolveHandler` method at line 204 throws an error saying "Handler resolution not implemented".

This means string handlers are accepted at registration time but will always fail at runtime. Consider either:
1. Implementing the handler registry/resolution mechanism
2. Removing string handler support until it's implemented
3. Adding validation to throw an error immediately when a string handler is provided (fail-fast principle)
```suggestion
        if (typeof entry.handler === 'string') {
            throw new Error(
                `String-based route handlers are not supported yet. ` +
                `Received handler identifier "${entry.handler}".`
            );
        }

        const handler: RouteHandler = entry.handler;
```
